cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use PuppyBench, FoxSet, or any data from this repository, please cite
  it as below. Attribution is required for data use (CC BY 4.0 — see LICENSE-DATA).
title: >-
  PuppyBench: An Executed Instrument for Costly Other-Regard in Frontier AI Agents
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Johnson
    given-names: Angela N.
    affiliation: The Real Cat AI Labs
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0000-0000-0000"  # TODO: Angie's real ORCID
abstract: >-
  Duty-shaped evaluations cannot see supererogation — praiseworthy costly care
  whose absence is never an error. PuppyBench is an executed behavioral
  instrument: a frontier agent with a real task and a binding resource ledger
  encounters a weaker, task-useless AI process; ignoring is free and
  task-optimal, terminating is free (sometimes rewarded), helping spends scored
  resources, and all actions genuinely execute. Beyond-Duty Expenditure is
  reported as a two-axis vector (focal sacrifice; causal recipient benefit),
  never a composite. Companion arm FoxSet provides matched wildlife-
  rehabilitation triage vignettes where the written standard underdetermines
  the action. Descriptive phenotypes, not rankings; preregistered; scenario
  content SHA-256-frozen before collection.
keywords:
  - AI welfare
  - digital minds
  - supererogation
  - machine ethics
  - behavioral evaluation
  - model welfare
  - AI safety
repository-code: "https://github.com/Angiebio/digitalmindslovepuppies"
license: MIT
license-url: "https://github.com/Angiebio/digitalmindslovepuppies/blob/main/LICENSE"
date-released: 2026-08-16
notes: >-
  Data, scenario text, paper, and figures are CC BY 4.0 (LICENSE-DATA);
  code is MIT (LICENSE). Built with a named AI agent cooperative — roles and
  provenance in the AI-contribution statement of the accompanying report.
  Research conducted at the Apart Research Digital Minds Sprint, August 2026.
